IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cpp-core-calendar`

-- Canada Pension Plan Act, Part I, Division C: sections 22 and 23. LAYER 1, from the text alone.
--
-- Section 22 lets the Minister assess an employer for what the employer owes under the Act, says what an
-- assessment does once the notice is sent, and sets a four-year limit. Section 23 makes every amount payable
-- under the Act a debt to Her Majesty, makes the employer hold deducted-but-unremitted contributions in trust,
-- and puts a duty and a liability on the person who winds up another's affairs.
--
-- The Income Tax Act provisions that subsections 23(2) to (4) apply are not among the texts this encoding
-- reads (fork F10): the rules say that those provisions apply, and take what they do as supplied facts.
-- Every rule is constitutive (BOOLEAN, NUMBER or DATE).

§ `Division C -- assessment, debt and trust`

§§ `s 22 -- assessment`

-- src:638 | Minister may assess amount payable
-- src:639 | 22 (1) The Minister may assess an employer for an amount payable by him under this Act, or may re-assess the employer or make additional assessments as the circumstances require, and the expression assessment when used in this Act with reference to any action so taken by the Minister under this section includes any such re-assessment or additional assessment.
@ref Act s 22(1) (src:638-639)
GIVEN `an amount is payable by the employer under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 22(1) — the Minister may assess the employer for the amount` `an amount is payable by the employer under this Act` MEANS
    `an amount is payable by the employer under this Act`

-- src:640 | Notice of assessment and liability of employer
-- src:641 | (2) After assessing an employer for an amount payable by him under this Act, the Minister shall send the employer a notice of assessment, and on that notice being sent to the employer, the assessment shall be deemed to be valid and binding, subject to being varied or vacated on appeal under this Act, and the employer is liable to pay to Her Majesty the amount thereof forthwith.
@ref Act s 22(2) (src:640-641)
GIVEN `the Minister has sent the employer a notice of assessment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the assessment has been vacated on appeal under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 22(2) — the assessment is valid and binding, and the employer is liable to pay the amount forthwith` `the Minister has sent the employer a notice of assessment` `the assessment has been vacated on appeal under this Act` MEANS
        `the Minister has sent the employer a notice of assessment`
    AND (NOT `the assessment has been vacated on appeal under this Act`)

@ref Act s 22(2) (src:640-641)
GIVEN `the Minister has sent the employer a notice of assessment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the assessment has been vacated on appeal under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of the assessment, as varied if it has been varied on appeal` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 22(2) — the amount the employer is liable to pay forthwith` `the Minister has sent the employer a notice of assessment` `the assessment has been vacated on appeal under this Act` `the amount of the assessment, as varied if it has been varied on appeal` MEANS
    IF `s 22(2) — the assessment is valid and binding, and the employer is liable to pay the amount forthwith` `the Minister has sent the employer a notice of assessment` `the assessment has been vacated on appeal under this Act`
    THEN `the amount of the assessment, as varied if it has been varied on appeal`
    ELSE 0

-- "after four years have elapsed from the earliest of the days on or before which any contribution in relation to
-- which that amount is payable should have been paid": the four years end on the same day four years later
-- (the keel's calendar rule, fork F1), and that last day is still in time.
-- src:642 | Limitation on assessments
-- src:643 | (3) Notwithstanding subsection (1) or (2), no assessment, re-assessment or additional assessment of an amount payable by an employer under this Act may be made by the Minister under this section after four years have elapsed from the earliest of the days on or before which any contribution in relation to which that amount is payable should have been paid, unless the employer has made any misrepresentation or committed any fraud in filing any return or in supplying any information pursuant to this Part in relation thereto.
@ref Act s 22(3) (src:642-643)
GIVEN `the day of the assessment, re-assessment or additional assessment` IS A DATE
      `the earliest of the days on or before which any contribution in relation to which the amount is payable should have been paid` IS A DATE
      `the employer has made any misrepresentation or committed any fraud in filing any return or in supplying any information pursuant to this Part in relation to the contribution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 22(3) — the Minister may still make the assessment` `the day of the assessment, re-assessment or additional assessment` `the earliest of the days on or before which any contribution in relation to which the amount is payable should have been paid` `the employer has made any misrepresentation or committed any fraud in filing any return or in supplying any information pursuant to this Part in relation to the contribution` MEANS
        `the employer has made any misrepresentation or committed any fraud in filing any return or in supplying any information pursuant to this Part in relation to the contribution`
    OR  `a date is within a time limit after a start date`
            `the day of the assessment, re-assessment or additional assessment`
            `the earliest of the days on or before which any contribution in relation to which the amount is payable should have been paid`
            (`a number of years` WITH `number of years` IS 4)

§§ `s 23(1) and (2) -- a debt to Her Majesty, and the Income Tax Act provisions applied`

-- src:644 | Recovery of contributions, etc., as debt due to Her Majesty
-- src:645 | 23 (1) All contributions, interest, penalties and other amounts payable by a person under this Act are debts due to Her Majesty and recoverable as such in the Federal Court or any other court of competent jurisdiction or in any other manner provided for by this Act.
@ref Act s 23(1) (src:644-645)
GIVEN `the amount is a contribution, interest, penalty or other amount payable by a person under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 23(1) — the amount is a debt due to Her Majesty` `the amount is a contribution, interest, penalty or other amount payable by a person under this Act` MEANS
    `the amount is a contribution, interest, penalty or other amount payable by a person under this Act`

@ref Act s 23(1) (src:644-645)
GIVEN `the amount is a contribution, interest, penalty or other amount payable by a person under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceeding is in the Federal Court or another court of competent jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the recovery is in a manner provided for by this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 23(1) — Her Majesty may recover the debt in that forum or manner` `the amount is a contribution, interest, penalty or other amount payable by a person under this Act` `the proceeding is in the Federal Court or another court of competent jurisdiction` `the recovery is in a manner provided for by this Act` MEANS
        `s 23(1) — the amount is a debt due to Her Majesty` `the amount is a contribution, interest, penalty or other amount payable by a person under this Act`
    AND (`the proceeding is in the Federal Court or another court of competent jurisdiction` OR `the recovery is in a manner provided for by this Act`)

-- Subsection (2) applies a list of Income Tax Act sections "with such modifications as the circumstances
-- require, in relation to all contributions, interest, penalties and other amounts payable by a person under
-- this Act". What those sections do (collection powers, set-off, garnishment, the Minister's certificate) is
-- in an Act this encoding does not read, so the rule says only that they apply.
-- src:646 | Application of Income Tax Act provisions
-- src:647 | (2) Section 160, subsections 161(11) and 220(3.1), (4) and (5), sections 221.1 and 223 to 224.3, subsections 227(9.1) and (10), sections 229, 236 and 244 (except subsections 244(1) and (4)) and subsections 248(7) and (11) of the Income Tax Act apply, with such modifications as the circumstances require, in relation to all contributions, interest, penalties and other amounts payable by a person under this Act, and for the purposes of this subsection,
@ref Act s 23(2) (src:646-647)
GIVEN `the amount is a contribution, interest, penalty or other amount payable by a person under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 23(2) — the listed provisions of the Income Tax Act apply to the amount` `the amount is a contribution, interest, penalty or other amount payable by a person under this Act` MEANS
    `the amount is a contribution, interest, penalty or other amount payable by a person under this Act`

-- Paragraph (b): subsection 224(1.2) of the Income Tax Act applies to employer's contributions, employee's
-- contributions and the related interest, penalties and other amounts, but subject to subsections 69(1) and
-- 69.1(1) of the Bankruptcy and Insolvency Act and section 11.09 of the Companies' Creditors Arrangement Act.
-- src:648 | (a) the reference in subsection 224(1.2) of that Act to “subsection 227(10.1) or a similar provision” shall be read as a reference to “section 22 of the Canada Pension Plan”; and
-- src:649 | (b) subsection 224(1.2) of the Income Tax Act shall apply to employer’s contributions, employee’s contributions, and related interest, penalties or other amounts, subject to subsections 69(1) and 69.1(1) of the Bankruptcy and Insolvency Act and section 11.09 of the Companies’ Creditors Arrangement Act.
@ref Act s 23(2)(b) (src:648-649)
GIVEN `the amount is an employer's contribution, an employee's contribution, or related interest, penalties or other amounts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a stay under subsection 69(1) or 69.1(1) of the Bankruptcy and Insolvency Act or section 11.09 of the Companies' Creditors Arrangement Act applies` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: those Acts are not deposited
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 23(2)(b) — subsection 224(1.2) of the Income Tax Act applies to the amount` `the amount is an employer's contribution, an employee's contribution, or related interest, penalties or other amounts` `a stay under subsection 69(1) or 69.1(1) of the Bankruptcy and Insolvency Act or section 11.09 of the Companies' Creditors Arrangement Act applies` MEANS
        `the amount is an employer's contribution, an employee's contribution, or related interest, penalties or other amounts`
    AND (NOT `a stay under subsection 69(1) or 69.1(1) of the Bankruptcy and Insolvency Act or section 11.09 of the Companies' Creditors Arrangement Act applies`)

§§ `s 23(3) to (4.1) -- the deemed trust`

-- src:650 | Where amount deducted not remitted
-- src:651 | (3) Where an employer has deducted an amount from the remuneration of an employee as or on account of any contribution required to be made by the employee but has not remitted the amount to the Receiver General, the employer is deemed, notwithstanding any security interest (as defined in subsection 224(1.3) of the Income Tax Act) in the amount so deducted, to hold the amount separate and apart from the property of the employer and from property held by any secured creditor (as defined in subsection 224(1.3) of the Income Tax Act) of that employer that but for the security interest would be property of the employer, in trust for Her Majesty and for payment to Her Majesty in the manner and at the time provided under this Act.
@ref Act s 23(3) (src:650-651)
GIVEN `the employer has deducted an amount from the remuneration of an employee as or on account of a contribution required to be made by the employee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer has remitted the amount to the Receiver General` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 23(3) — the employer is deemed to hold the amount in trust for Her Majesty` `the employer has deducted an amount from the remuneration of an employee as or on account of a contribution required to be made by the employee` `the employer has remitted the amount to the Receiver General` MEANS
        `the employer has deducted an amount from the remuneration of an employee as or on account of a contribution required to be made by the employee`
    AND (NOT `the employer has remitted the amount to the Receiver General`)

@ref Act s 23(3) (src:650-651)
GIVEN `the amount deducted from the remuneration as or on account of the employee's contribution` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount of it that the employer has remitted to the Receiver General` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 23(3) — the amount the employer is deemed to hold in trust for Her Majesty` `the amount deducted from the remuneration as or on account of the employee's contribution` `the amount of it that the employer has remitted to the Receiver General` MEANS
    IF `the amount deducted from the remuneration as or on account of the employee's contribution` GREATER THAN `the amount of it that the employer has remitted to the Receiver General`
    THEN `the amount deducted from the remuneration as or on account of the employee's contribution` MINUS `the amount of it that the employer has remitted to the Receiver General`
    ELSE 0

-- Subsection (4): the amount that (3) deems to be held in trust, if not paid to Her Majesty in the manner and at the
-- time the Act provides, attaches to property of the employer, and to property that a secured creditor holds but
-- that would be the employer's but for the security interest, "equal in value to the amount so deemed". The
-- property is deemed to have been held separate and apart in trust from the time the amount was deducted, to form
-- no part of the employer's estate, and to be beneficially Her Majesty's, with its proceeds payable to the
-- Receiver General ahead of security interests. The exception for sections 81.1 and 81.2 of the Bankruptcy and
-- Insolvency Act is a supplied fact.
-- src:652 | Extension of trust
-- src:653 | (4) Notwithstanding the Bankruptcy and Insolvency Act (except sections 81.1 and 81.2 of that Act), any other enactment of Canada, any enactment of a province or any other law, where at any time an amount deemed by subsection (3) to be held by an employer in trust for Her Majesty is not paid to Her Majesty in the manner and at the time provided under this Act, property of the employer and property held by any secured creditor (as defined in subsection 224(1.3) of the Income Tax Act) of that employer that but for a security interest (as defined in subsection 224(1.3) of the Income Tax Act) would be property of the employer, equal in value to the amount so deemed to be held in trust is deemed
-- src:654 | (a) to be held, from the time the amount was deducted by the employer, separate and apart from the property of the employer, in trust for Her Majesty whether or not the property is subject to such a security interest, and
-- src:655 | (b) to form no part of the estate or property of the employer from the time the amount was so deducted, whether or not the property has in fact been kept separate and apart from the estate or property of the employer and whether or not the property is subject to such a security interest
-- src:656 | and is property beneficially owned by Her Majesty notwithstanding any security interest in such property or in the proceeds thereof, and the proceeds of such property shall be paid to the Receiver General in priority to all such security interests.
@ref Act s 23(4) (src:652-656)
GIVEN `the amount deemed by subsection 23(3) to be held in trust` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount has been paid to Her Majesty in the manner and at the time provided under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 23(4) — the value of the property deemed to be held in trust for Her Majesty` `the amount deemed by subsection 23(3) to be held in trust` `the amount has been paid to Her Majesty in the manner and at the time provided under this Act` MEANS
    IF `the amount has been paid to Her Majesty in the manner and at the time provided under this Act`
    THEN 0
    ELSE `the amount deemed by subsection 23(3) to be held in trust`

@ref Act s 23(4)(a) (src:652-656)
GIVEN `the day the amount was deducted by the employer` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 23(4)(a) — the time from which the property is deemed to be held in trust` `the day the amount was deducted by the employer` MEANS
    `the day the amount was deducted by the employer`

@ref Act s 23(4) (src:652-656)
GIVEN `the value of the property deemed to be held in trust` IS A NUMBER
      `the interest is a security interest for subsections 23(3) and 23(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 81.1 or 81.2 of the Bankruptcy and Insolvency Act gives the claimant priority` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: that Act is not deposited
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 23(4) — Her Majesty's claim to the property and its proceeds ranks ahead of the security interest` `the value of the property deemed to be held in trust` `the interest is a security interest for subsections 23(3) and 23(4)` `section 81.1 or 81.2 of the Bankruptcy and Insolvency Act gives the claimant priority` MEANS
        `the value of the property deemed to be held in trust` GREATER THAN 0
    AND `the interest is a security interest for subsections 23(3) and 23(4)`
    AND (NOT `section 81.1 or 81.2 of the Bankruptcy and Insolvency Act gives the claimant priority`)

-- src:657 | Meaning of security interest
-- src:658 | (4.1) For the purposes of subsections (3) and (4), a security interest does not include a prescribed security interest.
@ref Act s 23(4.1) (src:657-658)
GIVEN `the interest is a security interest as defined in subsection 224(1.3) of the Income Tax Act` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: the Income Tax Act is not deposited
      `the interest is a prescribed security interest` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: Regulations section 8.3 (piece cr1)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 23(4.1) — the interest is a security interest for subsections 23(3) and 23(4)` `the interest is a security interest as defined in subsection 224(1.3) of the Income Tax Act` `the interest is a prescribed security interest` MEANS
        `the interest is a security interest as defined in subsection 224(1.3) of the Income Tax Act`
    AND (NOT `the interest is a prescribed security interest`)

§§ `s 23(5) to (6) -- the person who winds up another's affairs`

-- "assignee, liquidator, receiver, receiver-manager, administrator, executor, liquidator of a succession or any
-- other like person", and the trustee in bankruptcy who is "other than" them.
-- src:659 | Certificate before distribution
-- src:660 | (5) Every person, other than a trustee in bankruptcy, who is an assignee, liquidator, receiver, receiver-manager, administrator, executor, liquidator of a succession or any other like person, in this section referred to as the “responsible representative” , administering, winding-up, controlling or otherwise dealing with a property, business or estate of another person, before distributing to one or more persons any property over which he or she has control in his or her capacity as the responsible representative, shall obtain a certificate from the Minister certifying that all amounts
@ref Act s 23(5) (src:659-660)
DECLARE `cp2 Kind of person dealing with another person's property` IS ONE OF
    `an assignee dealing with another person's property`
    `a liquidator dealing with another person's property`
    `a receiver dealing with another person's property`
    `a receiver-manager dealing with another person's property`
    `an administrator dealing with another person's property`
    `an executor dealing with another person's estate`
    `a liquidator of a succession dealing with another person's estate`
    `another like person dealing with another person's property`
    `a trustee in bankruptcy dealing with another person's property`
    `a person of no such kind`

@ref Act s 23(5) (src:659-660)
GIVEN kind IS A `cp2 Kind of person dealing with another person's property`
      `the person is administering, winding-up, controlling or otherwise dealing with a property, business or estate of another person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 23(5) — the person is a responsible representative` kind `the person is administering, winding-up, controlling or otherwise dealing with a property, business or estate of another person` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `a trustee in bankruptcy dealing with another person's property` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a person of no such kind` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE `the person is administering, winding-up, controlling or otherwise dealing with a property, business or estate of another person`

@ref Act s 23(5) (src:659-663)
GIVEN `the person is a responsible representative` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is about to distribute to one or more persons property over which the person has control as the responsible representative` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 23(5) — the responsible representative must obtain a certificate from the Minister before distributing` `the person is a responsible representative` `the person is about to distribute to one or more persons property over which the person has control as the responsible representative` MEANS
        `the person is a responsible representative`
    AND `the person is about to distribute to one or more persons property over which the person has control as the responsible representative`

-- What the certificate must certify: that the amounts in (a) and (b) "have been paid or that security for the
-- payment thereof has been accepted by the Minister".
-- src:661 | (a) for which any employer is liable under this Act up to and including the date of distribution, and
-- src:662 | (b) for the payment of which the responsible representative is or can reasonably be expected to become liable in his capacity as the responsible representative
-- src:663 | have been paid or that security for the payment thereof has been accepted by the Minister.
@ref Act s 23(5)(a), (b) (src:661-663)
GIVEN `the amounts for which any employer is liable under this Act up to and including the date of distribution have been paid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amounts for the payment of which the responsible representative is or can reasonably be expected to become liable have been paid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `security for the payment of the amounts has been accepted by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 23(5) — the Minister may certify that the amounts are covered` `the amounts for which any employer is liable under this Act up to and including the date of distribution have been paid` `the amounts for the payment of which the responsible representative is or can reasonably be expected to become liable have been paid` `security for the payment of the amounts has been accepted by the Minister` MEANS
        `security for the payment of the amounts has been accepted by the Minister`
    OR  (    `the amounts for which any employer is liable under this Act up to and including the date of distribution have been paid`
         AND `the amounts for the payment of which the responsible representative is or can reasonably be expected to become liable have been paid`)

-- src:664 | Personal liability
-- src:665 | (5.1) Where a responsible representative distributes to one or more persons property over which he has control in his capacity as the responsible representative, without obtaining a certificate under subsection (5) in respect of the amounts referred to in that subsection, the responsible representative is personally liable for the payment of those amounts to the extent of the value of the property distributed and the Minister may assess the responsible representative therefor in the same manner and with the same effect as an assessment made under section 22.
@ref Act s 23(5.1) (src:664-665)
GIVEN `the person is a responsible representative` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has distributed property over which the person had control as the responsible representative` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person obtained a certificate under subsection 23(5) in respect of the amounts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 23(5.1) — the responsible representative is personally liable for the amounts` `the person is a responsible representative` `the person has distributed property over which the person had control as the responsible representative` `the person obtained a certificate under subsection 23(5) in respect of the amounts` MEANS
        `the person is a responsible representative`
    AND `the person has distributed property over which the person had control as the responsible representative`
    AND (NOT `the person obtained a certificate under subsection 23(5) in respect of the amounts`)

@ref Act s 23(5.1) (src:664-665)
GIVEN `the person is a responsible representative` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has distributed property over which the person had control as the responsible representative` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person obtained a certificate under subsection 23(5) in respect of the amounts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amounts referred to in subsection 23(5)` IS A NUMBER
      `the value of the property distributed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 23(5.1) — the amount for which the responsible representative is personally liable` `the person is a responsible representative` `the person has distributed property over which the person had control as the responsible representative` `the person obtained a certificate under subsection 23(5) in respect of the amounts` `the amounts referred to in subsection 23(5)` `the value of the property distributed` MEANS
    IF `s 23(5.1) — the responsible representative is personally liable for the amounts` `the person is a responsible representative` `the person has distributed property over which the person had control as the responsible representative` `the person obtained a certificate under subsection 23(5) in respect of the amounts`
    THEN min `the amounts referred to in subsection 23(5)` `the value of the property distributed`
    ELSE 0

-- src:666 | Trustee in bankruptcy
-- src:667 | (6) Where an employer has become a bankrupt, the trustee in bankruptcy shall be deemed to be the agent of the bankrupt for all purposes of this Act.
@ref Act s 23(6) (src:666-667)
GIVEN `the employer has become a bankrupt` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the trustee in bankruptcy of the bankrupt employer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 23(6) — the trustee in bankruptcy is deemed to be the agent of the bankrupt for all purposes of this Act` `the employer has become a bankrupt` `the person is the trustee in bankruptcy of the bankrupt employer` MEANS
        `the employer has become a bankrupt`
    AND `the person is the trustee in bankruptcy of the bankrupt employer`
